From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cloud Office <me@diegonmarcos.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 00:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cloud-office: a failing make must say why in the build log

generateCoolReleaseAssets is the COOL web-UI build, and it is the one
task this app cannot skip: patches/0001 edits browser/, so assets/dist
has to come from this tree rather than from the pinned APK. It is also
the only task in the Android build that can fail without saying anything.

providers.exec CAPTURES the subprocess's stdout and stderr into the
ExecOutput it returns and forwards neither to Gradle's logger. The two
calls here then threw the captured streams away by asking only for
.result.get(), so make's exit status arrived and make's reason did not.
Run 35038703895 is what that costs: 78 of 78 Android tasks executed,
:lib:generateCoolReleaseAssets failed 37 seconds in, and the whole
1,270-line job log carried a Gradle stack trace, the string "Process
'command 'make'' finished with non-zero exit value 2", and not one line
of make's own output. Re-running with --info, which the "Try:" block
suggests, would not have helped either: these streams never reach the
logger at any level, so there is no verbosity that prints them.

An engine step that hides the diagnostics of the tool it drives cannot
be debugged except by guessing, and every guess here costs a run that
fetches a 2 GB Gerrit tree. So both tasks now go through one helper that
sets ignoreExitValue, reads the two streams, prints them when the exit
status is non-zero, and only then fails the build with the command and
the code in the message. The debug variant gets it too — a task that is
only legible in one of its two forms is the same bug half-fixed.

Nothing about WHAT is built changes: same make, same -C, same
DIST_FOLDER and BUNDLE arguments, same clean-then-build order.
---
 android/lib/build.gradle | 46 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/android/lib/build.gradle b/android/lib/build.gradle
index bfd88f7..2784fe4 100644
--- a/android/lib/build.gradle
+++ b/android/lib/build.gradle
@@ -367,25 +367,47 @@ preBuild.dependsOn 'createRCfiles',
         'createFullConfig',
         'copyBrandTheme'
 
+// WHEN make FAILS, ITS OWN ERROR HAS TO BE IN THE BUILD LOG.
+//
+// providers.exec CAPTURES the subprocess's stdout and stderr into the returned
+// ExecOutput and forwards neither of them to Gradle's logger, so a plain
+// `.result.get()` throws with "Process 'command 'make'' finished with non-zero
+// exit value 2" and DISCARDS the npm, tsc or eslint diagnostic that says what
+// is actually wrong. Run 35038703895 died exactly there: 78 of 78 Android
+// tasks ran, this one failed 37 seconds in, and the entire job log held a
+// Gradle stack trace and not one line of make's output. Running Gradle with
+// --info does not help, because those streams never reach the logger at any
+// level. ignoreExitValue is what lets them be read, and printed, before the
+// build is failed.
+def coolMake = { List<String> args ->
+    String browser = "${rootProject.layout.buildDirectory.get()}/../../browser".toString()
+    logger.lifecycle("cool: make -C {} {}", browser, args.join(' '))
+    def run = providers.exec {
+        commandLine(['make', '-C', browser] + args)
+        ignoreExitValue = true
+    }
+    String out = run.standardOutput.asText.get()
+    String err = run.standardError.asText.get()
+    int code = run.result.get().exitValue
+    if (code != 0) {
+        logger.error("cool: make -C ${browser} ${args.join(' ')} exited ${code}; its output follows")
+        if (out) { logger.error(out) }
+        if (err) { logger.error(err) }
+        throw new GradleException("make -C ${browser} ${args.join(' ')} failed with exit ${code}")
+    }
+}
+
 tasks.register('generateCoolDebugAssets') {
     doLast {
-        providers.exec {
-            commandLine 'make', '-C', "${rootProject.layout.buildDirectory.get()}/../../browser", 'clean'
-        }.result.get()
-        providers.exec {
-            commandLine 'make', '-C', "${rootProject.layout.buildDirectory.get()}/../../browser", "DIST_FOLDER=${project.layout.projectDirectory}/src/debug/assets/dist", 'BUNDLE=DEBUG'
-        }.result.get()
+        coolMake(['clean'])
+        coolMake(["DIST_FOLDER=${project.layout.projectDirectory}/src/debug/assets/dist".toString(), 'BUNDLE=DEBUG'])
     }
 }
 
 tasks.register('generateCoolReleaseAssets') {
     doLast {
-        providers.exec {
-            commandLine 'make', '-C', "${rootProject.layout.buildDirectory.get()}/../../browser", 'clean'
-        }.result.get()
-        providers.exec {
-            commandLine 'make', '-C', "${rootProject.layout.buildDirectory.get()}/../../browser", "DIST_FOLDER=${project.layout.projectDirectory}/src/release/assets/dist", 'BUNDLE=RELEASE'
-        }.result.get()
+        coolMake(['clean'])
+        coolMake(["DIST_FOLDER=${project.layout.projectDirectory}/src/release/assets/dist".toString(), 'BUNDLE=RELEASE'])
     }
 }
 
